      "persona": "Whitehat Hacker",
      "taskMessage": "<b>Dr. Mira Sen:</b> UDP silence is ambiguous. A quiet service and a firewall drop can produce the same result, so keep the scanner's hedged label instead of reporting a closed port.",
      "taskInstructions": "Run <b>nmap -sU 10.42.18.73</b> in the terminal and read the state column of the UDP results.",
      "taskQuestion": "What does open|filtered mean in this UDP result?",
      "taskCompleteText": "<b>Dr. Mira Sen:</b> Correct. Open|filtered records uncertainty between a quiet service and a filtered response.",
      "answers": [
        "The scanner cannot tell a quiet open service from a filtered one.",
        "The service is confirmed exploitable on the listed UDP service port.",
        "The host is fully offline and answered nothing at all.",
        "UDP scanning falls outside the approved assessment scope."
